  "id": "change-effect",
  "term": "change effect",
  "definition": "In cognitive dissonance research, the change effect is the shift in a person’s attitude after engaging in behavior that goes against their original view, such as writing a counter-attitudinal essay. In the induced-compliance setting described here, greater attitude change was linked with more positive emotions and less change with more negative emotions.",
